{
  "name": "mask_quality",
  "how": "Soybean d97rjyk2tz single-seed images, the 2121 R2 rows (data/crops/manifest_soybean.csv). Four crop arms, all 224 px with pipeline/make_crops.masked_crop geometry (square, seed bbox 85 % of the side) and embedded with frozen facebook/dinov2-small (CLS + mean patch, pipeline/features.embed): current = chroma mask (existing features); fastsam = FastSAM-s (Ultralytics v8.3.0 weights, SHA-256 c9f78716...0844, AGPL-3.0) imgsz 640, conf 0.4 (retry 0.1), NMS IoU 0.9, retina masks, mask with the highest IoU vs the chroma mask among masks covering 0.5-90 % of the image, holes filled, largest component, background painted FILL; fastsam_dil = that mask dilated by 4 % of the seed's equivalent diameter; nomask = same square crop around the FastSAM seed with the real background kept. Mask quality: IoU of the FastSAM mask vs the chroma mask on every image; disagree = 1 - IoU > 0.10. Classifier: harness.FrozenLogReg. Protocol r2_fixed_split = experiments/r2_per_class.evaluate unchanged (fit split=train, C from [0.01, 0.03, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0, 3.0] by macro F1 on val eval_rep, refit, score test eval_rep, multi_seed excluded, 19 test bursts). Protocol cv5_bursts = StratifiedGroupKFold(5, shuffle, seed 0) over bursts on all rows (train+val+test), C from [0.01, 0.1, 1.0] by inner grouped 3-fold CV, out-of-fold predictions on eval_rep non-multi-seed crops pooled; folds identical across arms. F1 CIs: percentile bootstrap over bursts, 2000 resamples, seed 0. Paired comparisons (arm minus current) on identical eval crops: the same burst resample scores both arms (2000, seed 0), 95 % percentile CI of the difference; McNemar exact test on per-crop correctness.",
